t discusses metastatic small cell carcinoma of the lung and the specific immunohistochemical markers (TTF1 positive, CDX2 negative) that suggest a lung origin.\n- Predicted Diagnostic Reasons are about acute appendicitis and perforated diverticulitis.\n- There are no statements in the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons that mention small cell carcinoma, lung origin, TTF1, or CDX2.\n- Pros: None.\n- Cons: No overlap in medical conditions, specific tumor types, diagnostic methods, or specific markers.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\nThere are no matching statements between the Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons and the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The groundtruth reasons are focused on specific cancer diagnoses and immunohistochemical findings, while the predicted reasons are focused on acute appendicitis and perforated diverticulitis based on clinical symptoms and CT findings.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
