  "cd7ad616291e3dccbd2bfdb2c174f8241137d88aa5ba595076739b4066e4eac0": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\n1. List all statements from Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons and Predicted Diagnostic Reasons.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n- Statement 1: \"Phyllodes tumor was excluded by its characteristic pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia on histology — “glands were lined by bilayered epithelium with pericanalicular pattern of fibroadenoma and absence of cytological atypia.”\"\n- Statement 2: \"Virginal hypertrophy was excluded by the finding of a discrete, well‐encapsulated tumor rather than diffuse glandular enlargement — “the specimen was sent for histopathological examination which showed well encapsulated tumor with hyperplasia of both epithelial and stromal components.”\"\n- Statement 3: \"Adenocarcinoma was excluded by the absence of cytological atypia on histopathology — “absence of cytological atypia.”\"\n- Statement 4: \"Tuberculosis was excluded by normal inflammatory markers and imaging — “Chest X-ray was normal.”\"\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons (statements from evidence lines):\n- Predicted 1: \"The patient's symptoms and examination results, including a well-circumscribed, firm, non-tender, mobile lump, are consistent with a diagnosis of fibroadenoma. Ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology also support this diagnosis.\"\n- Predicted 2: \"The patient's symptoms and examination results, including a well-circumscribed, firm, non-tender, mobile lump, are consistent with fibroadenoma. Ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology also suggest fibroadenoma.\"\n- Predicted 3: \"The patient's presentation of a rapidly enlarging, well-circumscribed, firm, non-tender, and mobile lump, along with ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology results, strongly supports the diagnosis of fibroadenoma, which is a common benign breast tumor, especially in young women.\"\n- Predicted 4: \"Given the patient's age, a juvenile fibroadenoma is a possible diagnosis, as these tumors are more common in younger women and can present with rapid growth.\"\n- Predicted 5: \"Given the patient's age and the characteristics of the lump, juvenile fibroadenoma is a plausible diagnosis. It is a type of fibroadenoma that occurs in younger women and can present as a rapidly growing, large mass.\"\n\n2. For each statement in Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons, consider potential matches from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n\n- Groundtruth 1: Mentions exclusion of phyllodes tumor based on pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia. Predicted statements do not mention phyllodes tumor, pericanalicular pattern, or absence of atypia. They only describe clinical features and imaging support for fibroadenoma. No match.\n- Groundtruth 2: Mentions exclusion of virginal hypertrophy based on discrete, well-encapsulated tumor vs. diffuse enlargement. Predicted statements mention \"well-circumscribed\" but not \"well-encapsulated\" explicitly, and do not compare to diffuse enlargement. No match.\n- Groundtruth 3: Mentions exclusion of adenocarcinoma based on absence of cytological atypia. Predicted statements do not mention cytological atypia or adenocarcinoma. No match.\n- Groundtruth 4: Mentions exclusion of tuberculosis based on normal chest X-ray and inflammatory markers. Predicted statements do not mention tuberculosis, chest X-ray, or inflammatory markers. No match.\n\n3. Summary of matching decisions: No predicted statement matches any groundtruth statement. All four groundtruth statements have zero matches.\n\n4. JSON output: For each groundtruth statement (1-4), the corresponding array is empty.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n\n<output>\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n</output>",
    "prompt_id": "mcr.reasoning_recall"
